-- title:
--   Places centred at a smooth special point with prescribed value
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field and $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring which is a henselian local ring, is not all of $L$, and satisfies the rank-one condition that for all $a, b \in A$ with $a$ in the maximal ideal and $b \neq 0$ there is $n \in \mathbb{N}$ with $b \mid a^{n}$. Let $F$ be a field, essentially of finite type over $L$, with `IsCurveOver L F`: every nonzero $f \in F$ has a degree-zero divisor recording $\operatorname{ord}_v f$ at all places $v$ of $F/L$, each place of $F/L$ has residue field finite over $L$, and $\Omega_{F/L}$ is free of rank one over $F$. Let $X$ be an integral scheme and $\mathrm{toBase} : X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ proper, flat and locally of finite presentation, and let $\varphi : F \cong X.\mathrm{functionField}$ be a ring isomorphism carrying, for each $a \in A$, the image of $a$ in $F$ to the image of $a$ under the canonical map `SemistableModel.baseToFunctionField toBase`. Let $x \in X$ lie over the closed point of $A$, admit no proper specialisation (every $y$ with $x \rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$), and lie in the smooth locus of $\mathrm{toBase}$; let $\eta \neq x$ be a further point over the closed point with $\eta \rightsquigarrow x$. Let $Fbar$ be a field over the residue field of $A$ and $R$ a `RegularProlongation A F Fbar`, that is, a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ meeting $L$ exactly in $A$, together with a surjective homomorphism $R.\mathrm{residue}$ to $Fbar$ with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$ and such that every nonzero element of $F$ becomes, after scaling by some element of $L$, an integer with nonzero residue; assume the subring underlying $R.\mathrm{integers}$ is $\mathcal{O}_{X,\eta}$ viewed in $F$ through $\varphi$. Put $S := \mathcal{O}_{X,x}$ viewed in $F$ through $\varphi$, and assume: the image of $A$ in $F$ lies in $S$; $Q$ is a place of $Fbar$ over the residue field of $A$ (a proper valuation subring containing the base field which is a principal ideal ring) which is rational, i.e. the residue field of $Q$ is generated by the residue field of $A$; every $f \in S$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $R.\mathrm{residue}(f)$ in the valuation subring of $Q$; for $f \in S$ lying in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, $f$ is a unit of $S$ if and only if $\operatorname{ord}_Q R.\mathrm{residue}(f) = 0$ and $R.\mathrm{residue}(f) \neq 0$; and $T \in S$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $\operatorname{ord}_Q R.\mathrm{residue}(T) = 1$. The conclusion is that for every $c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ one has $T \neq c$ in $F$, and there is a place $P$ of $F/L$ such that every $g \in S$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(g) \in A$, this value being a unit of $A$ exactly when $g$ is invertible in $S$; moreover $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(T) = c$, and every $s \in S$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(s) = 0$ is of the form $(T - c)s'$ with $s' \in S$.
--
--   This is the construction of $L$-rational points (places of $F/L$) specialising to a smooth closed point $x$ of the special fibre with prescribed value $c$ of a coordinate $T$ at $x$: the centre of the resulting place is the principal ideal $(T-c)S$ of the local ring $S = \mathcal{O}_{X,x}$, the section $S \to A$ with $T \mapsto c$ existing because $A$ is henselian. It feeds the identification of $\mathcal{O}_{X,x}$ inside $R.\mathrm{integers}$ by valuation-theoretic conditions in [`AlgebraicCurve.mem_localRing_of_mem_integers_of_forall_mem_valuationSubring_of_mem_smoothLocus`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.mem_localRing_of_mem_integers_of_forall_mem_valuationSubring_of_mem_smoothLocus), and is proved from the existence of such a section together with the passage from a section to a place.
